  "notes": "LayerDriver test fixture: US ANSI 104-key set (positions 1-104, identical to test-keymap-us104.json) plus 6 JIS-specific input keys appended at positions 105-110 (KC_ZKHK, KC_RO, KC_KANA, KC_JYEN, KC_HENK, KC_MHEN). Note on the '109-key' naming: real 109-key JIS keyboards typically have one of these JIS keys sharing a physical slot with a US-layout key (commonly KC_ZKHK sharing the grave/tilde corner, scancode 0x29 in this tool), so a specific physical board may only have 109 distinct keys rather than this fixture's 110 calibration slots. If your board only has 109 physical keys, press the same physical key twice when calibration reaches the merged slot (harmless -- both slots just resolve to the same scancode); this fixture prioritizes exercising all 6 JIS keycodes distinctly over matching one exact vendor's key count. Layer 1 behavior for positions 1-104 is identical to test-keymap-us104.json (MO(1) demo on position 71, F-key demo on the number row, Esc demo on Q); positions 105-110 (the JIS keys) are transparent on layer 1. See driver/KeymapTool/samples/README.md for the full ordered key list.",
